.TH SPEECHNOTES 1 "2026-11-18" "speechnotes 0.1.0-alpha.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
speechnotes \- notes, books and text-to-speech for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B speechnotes
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B speechnotes
is a GTK4 notes app with a full text-to-speech stack and a book reader.
Run without arguments it opens the graphical app. It also ships a headless
CLI: every subcommand below works without a display, so notes, books and
speech can be driven from scripts and servers.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-selftest
Run every core invariant (dates, chunking, stores, sanitizers) and exit
non-zero on the first failure. The batch gate for CI.
.TP
.BR \-\-speak " " \fITEXT\fR
Synthesize \fITEXT\fR through a speech engine to the default audio sink.
Accepts
.B \-\-engine
(\fIespeak\fR, \fIkokoro\fR, \fInano-edge-tts\fR, \fIsupertonic\fR,
\fIphonon\fR),
.B \-\-voice
and
.BR \-\-switch " " \fIENGINE\fR
(hot-switch the live session).
.TP
.BR \-\-engines
List the available speech engines and voices, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-receive
Serve the BookDrop receiver headless (LocalSend-compatible; LAN TCP ports
53317\*(en53327). Landed files import into the library.
.TP
.BI \-\-import-book " FILE"
Import a book (epub, pdf, mobi/azw3/pdb, fb2, rtf, html/htmlz, pptx/ppt/
ppsx/potx, odp) into the library.
.TP
.BI \-\-import-note " FILE"
Import a note from a \fI.docx\fR or \fI.jex\fR file.
.TP
.BI \-\-import-audiobook " FILE"
Import an audiobook (\fI.m4b\fR, \fI.opus\fR, \fI.mp3\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-books
List the library's books (id, format, title).
.TP
.BI \-\-open-book " ID" " [" "PAGE" "]"
Open a book by id prefix (optionally at a page) in the GUI.
.TP
.BI \-\-read-book " ID"
Extract a book's text to stdout.
.TP
.BI \-\-play-audiobook " ID"
Play an imported audiobook through the library's player session.
.TP
.BI \-\-play-note " ID"
Synthesize a stored note to the default audio sink.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/speechnotes/
notes.json, notebooks.json, bookmarks.json, Books/, models/, Exports/
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/speechnotes/prefs.json
App preferences.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README and
.UR https://github.com/thesagezm/speechnotes-linux
.UE .
